--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UPSTREAM ATTRIBUTION THAT TRAVELS WITH THESE REPORTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every table in these reports compares this harness's own computed values against
reference values from third-party datasets that are themselves CC BY 4.0.
Redistributing these reports carries their attribution requirement as well:

  * Materials Project (CC BY 4.0) -- reference energies, hull distances and
    structures. A. Jain et al., APL Materials 1, 011002 (2013).
    doi:10.1063/1.4812323

  * Matbench Discovery / WBM (CC BY 4.0) -- the calibration and test material
    sets. J. Riebesell et al., Nature Machine Intelligence (2025),
    arXiv:2308.14920. H.-C. Wang, S. Botti, M. A. L. Marques,
    npj Comput. Mater. 7, 12 (2021).

Changes were made: all values reported here are computed by this harness from the
above sources and are not the sources' own published numbers.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY VALUES QUOTED IN THESE REPORTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Where a report quotes experimental lattice constants, those measured values come
from Lucero, Henderson & Scuseria, J. Phys.: Condens. Matter 24, 145504 (2012)
(Copyright IOP Publishing) and Csonka, Perdew et al., Phys. Rev. B 79, 155107
(2009) (Copyright American Physical Society), cited in place. Where a report
quotes published Matbench Discovery leaderboard metrics, those come from the
matbench-discovery repository (MIT, Copyright (c) 2022 Janosh Riebesell).

Those quoted third-party values are not licensed by this file. This project's
CC BY 4.0 grant covers its own text, analysis, tables and computed results.

The root NOTICE file carries the full attribution block.
